                    <msContents><!-- describe the intellectual content of an inscription -->
                        <summary>The inscription records the gift of the village of Derindha situated in Kolleḍā maṇḍāla by Rāṇaka Devapya, son of Rāṇaka Śāṅkilla, belonging to the Rāṣṭrakula in favour of Bhaṭṭaputra Vāmana son of Vāpilla belonging to the Agasti gotra, the Chāndoga caraṇa and the Āśīti pravara</summary> <!-- offers the possibility to give a summary of the inscription's content -->
                    </msContents>
